      <workList xml:id="workDesc_N20348">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e225222">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_N2034C">C2:001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="de">An dem hohen Geburthsfeste Sr. königl. Hoheit des durchlauchtigsten Fürsten und Herrn Friederichs entwarf folgendes Gedichte in tiefster Unterthänigkeit Johann Adolph Scheibe</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_N2035A">
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="_22">Crown Prince Frederik</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_24_0">
               <date isodate="1741" xml:id="date_01706b10">1741</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_24_0">
               <p xml:id="idm79">On the crown prince’s eighteenth birthday, 31 March 1741, Scheibe offered the present publication. However, it has not been possible to determine whether music was composed to the text. The title page only mentions Scheibe as the author of the poem, and, furthermore, the text does not include the usual divisions in terms of arias and recitatives found in the usual cantata booklets. It should also be remembered that Scheibe was known for writing his own librettos and even poems. On the other hand, it would be somewhat out of the ordinary if Scheibe had merely presented a poem rather than a cantata.</p>
            </history>
